{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1788666186277334001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"foulard-bald-chick","assignee":null,"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":2,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"b30140f50540412c176eb5b984ebdd441e2ba2290543a0ef6de4776b60c64051","event_uuid":"6a3063ee-b6ee-4faa-bb5e-a9a08958e70f","position":{"commit_sha":"6e37483798f6be926ae24c6405c40d1b1d60cb5a","position":"1788656878016369509-6a3063ee-b6ee-4faa-bb5e-a9a08958e70f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"269bf62848383dd8aa0d73e59bbe64c7f040a6b5f7c7dd2ec9b2d8b2923a0150","event_uuid":"952fc9e5-178d-47b5-b21d-ba71791a2078","position":{"commit_sha":"6df97f8de3d302297f6d29006b47626035005907","position":"1788656887377604003-952fc9e5-178d-47b5-b21d-ba71791a2078"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1788656878016369509,"creation_channel":"mcp","deps":[{"link_uuid":"952fc9e5-178d-47b5-b21d-ba71791a2078","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"5bba-45dd-3bfc-42f1"}],"description":"## Summary\n\n`infra/runbooks/nginx-edge-render.md` (shipped with change 2702) prescribes a source step that\n**cannot work on the host it documents**. An operator following it verbatim gets a hard failure at\nthe first command and has no stated recovery.\n\n## Observed\n\nThe runbook says to obtain the template with:\n\n```sh\ncd /opt/rebar && git fetch origin && git checkout origin/main -- infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template\n```\n\nRun on the Gerrit host, that produces:\n\n```\nfatal: not a git repository (or any of the parent directories): .git\n```\n\n`/opt/rebar` is an **rsync copy** of the tree, not a git checkout — it has no `.git` at all, so\nneither the `fetch` nor the `checkout` can run. The autodeploy process keeps its own clone\nelsewhere, at **`/var/lib/rebar/mirror`**, and that is the path the template must actually be read\nfrom.\n\n## Why this matters more than a typo\n\nThe runbook exists to apply nginx edge config, and the edge is **detect-only under autodeploy** —\nmerging a template change does not deploy it. So this runbook is the *only* documented path from a\nmerged nginx change to a live one. A first step that always fails makes the documented path\nunusable, and the failure mode is an operator improvising a render under incident pressure. That is\nhow I produced a bad render on the first attempt: substituting by hand through SSM, shell quoting\nmangled the interpolation and the output had `proxy_read_timeout` count=3 instead of 4.\n\n## What the runbook gets RIGHT (do not change this)\n\nIts verification step is what caught that bad render before I installed a no-op:\n\n```sh\ngrep -c proxy_read_timeout /etc/nginx/conf.d/rebar.conf   # expect 4\n```\n\nwith the explicit note that **\"a count of 3 means the render did not happen.\"** That check earned\nits keep on its first real use. Keep it exactly as it is.\n\n## Suggested fix\n\nReplace the source step with the mirror path, and make the runbook state *why* the obvious path is\nwrong so the next reader does not \"fix\" it back:\n\n```sh\n# /opt/rebar is an rsync COPY with no .git — read the template from the autodeploy clone.\ngit -C /var/lib/rebar/mirror fetch origin\ngit -C /var/lib/rebar/mirror show origin/main:infra/nginx/rebar.conf.template > /tmp/rebar.conf.tmpl\n```\n\nConfirm `/var/lib/rebar/mirror` is genuinely a git repo and is the autodeploy clone before\ncommitting to it in the doc — I observed it as the clone autodeploy maintains, but that should be\nverified rather than taken from this report.\n\n## Also worth recording in the runbook\n\nThe render leaves **one** unsubstituted `REVIEW_BOT_PORT` mention and that is **expected**, not a\nrender failure: it is line 6 of the template, `#     export REVIEW_BOT_PORT`, a bare name inside a\ncomment with no `${}`, which `sed 's|${REVIEW_BOT_PORT}|8000|g'` correctly does not match. Both\nfunctional occurrences (the `proxy_pass` and the `proxy_redirect`) do substitute. Saying so in the\nrunbook saves the next operator from chasing it mid-incident.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] AC1 The runbook's source step is executed successfully **on the host** as written in the\n      fix, and the transcript is recorded on this ticket. A step that is only reasoned about is\n      not verified — this bug exists precisely because the original step was plausible and untried.\n- [ ] AC2 The runbook states that `/opt/rebar` is an rsync copy and must not be used as a git\n      source, so the incorrect step is not reintroduced by someone \"simplifying\" the path.\n- [ ] AC3 The expected `unsubstituted=1` (the line-6 comment) is documented as normal, with the\n      reason, so it is not mistaken for a partial render.\n- [ ] AC4 The existing `grep -c proxy_read_timeout ... # expect 4` verification and its \"a count of\n      3 means the render did not happen\" note are preserved verbatim.\n\n## Constraints\n\nNever use `--force` or any gate bypass. `timeout` does not exist on this macOS host (it exits 127,\na silent no-op) — bound with `perl -e 'alarm N; exec @ARGV'`. Do not touch the shared main\ncheckout; do not `git stash` anywhere.","env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":3,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"08be-a081-7442-4ba7","ticket_type":"bug","title":"nginx-edge-render runbook's source step fails: /opt/rebar is an rsync copy, not a git checkout","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6a3063ee-b6ee-4faa-bb5e-a9a08958e70f","952fc9e5-178d-47b5-b21d-ba71791a2078"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1788666186277334001,"uuid":"6af323e8-87a5-4639-a400-f53564dac065"}